00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:24.160
<b>Mejiro McQueen</b>

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:22.750
How are you feeling?

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.160
Perfect, I'd say.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:26.670
You nervous or anything?

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:30.880
I do feel anxious about needing to win, yes.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.170
You've got a streak to protect, after all.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:37.110
I will run in a way that 
makes me fit to be your goal.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:38.390
Please, watch me.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.200
Okay.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.200
Good luck!

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:44.270
Running past the stands now is Mejiro Palmer.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.370
She's expected to attempt to outrun 
the competition once again.

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.270
Keep it hype, girl!

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:53.340
She's been voted fourth most popular. 
What do you think that implies, Hosoe-san?

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:56.350
In her last race, the 3,000-meter
 Hanshin Daishoten,

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:58.830
she managed to secure a splendid 
victory via outrunning.

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:00.460
We can expect to see
a great race from her.

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:03.360
And here we have two other racers 
who are looking to win big.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:06.410
Ikuno Dictus and Machikane Tannhäuser 
seem to be in good spirits.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:07.600
Good luck, you two.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:09.670
Iku Dis! Machi Tan!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.740
Machikane Tannhäuser is third most popular,

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:14.670
and has been gathering more and more 
attention from the fans lately.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:17.840
She's won her last two races, 
and has a lot of momentum.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:20.180
She's got a good chance at coming 
away with this spring's plaque.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.110
I bet she's got a
good race ahead of her.

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:25.250
And number one with a 
bullet is Mejiro McQueen!

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:29.190
I think it's fair to say that she's the 
horse girl closest to winning this race.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:10.980
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:10.980
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:16.980
As the G1 Spring Tennoushou fanfare plays, 
the horse girls are now entering the gate.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:19.120
You can do this, McQueen!

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:21.200
Please win for a third time!

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:23.410
Don't sweat this streak stuff!

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.260
That's kinda asking a lot.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:26.250
That's true.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:26.990
What's going on?

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.050
Huh?

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:29.530
What happened?

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:30.620
Hey...

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:33.000
She's not going in?

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.000
What's going on?

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:43.920
Oh, it looks like Mejiro McQueen 
hasn't entered the gate yet.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:45.510
That's odd.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:46.790
What the heck?

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:48.900
What's wrong with McQueen-san?

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:50.520
It's just like during her training.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:51.280
Seriously?

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:52.800
What's gotten into her?

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:54.270
McQueen...

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:57.560
McQueen-san...

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.750
<i>What is she, a wild animal?</i>

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:04.040
<i>It feels like she's ready to tear me apart.</i>

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:08.860
<i>But I have my own reasons 
for winning this race.</i>

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.290
Mejiro McQueen is finally inside the gate.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:13.670
Okay, there she goes!

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.290
Show them what you've got, McQueen!

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:17.650
It takes power and stamina in equal measure

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:20.430
to come out on top in this 3,200-meter 
trek around the Kyoto Racecourse.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:23.800
All 15 horse girls are now inside the gate.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.760
And now the Spring Tennoushou...

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:26.660
has...

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.260
begun!

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:30.970
Go, McQueen!

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:30.970
...san!

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:33.270
Iku Dis! Machi Tan!

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:34.700
McQueen!

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:35.770
McQueen!

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.770
Mejiro Palmer is in front, as expected.

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:40.030
<i>Got this!</i>

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.860
Time to outrun! Let's go!

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.040
Further out from the 
center is Mejiro McQueen,

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:46.270
who's sticking close behind Mejiro Palmer!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.530
Looking good, McQueen!

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:49.480
No...

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:50.430
What's wrong?

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:52.290
They just started!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.480
She can't start chasing Palmer this soon.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:56.310
That's right, she can't!

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:59.500
<i>No... it's not Palmer she's worried about.</i>

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.880
<i>I think it's...</i>

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.660
McQueen is currently in fourth place,

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:06.130
and following her closely is Rice Shower, 
whose black hair is trailing behind her.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.550
Rice has been on McQueen the whole time.

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:11.400
She's got her marked pretty clearly.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:13.520
But why not get behind her?

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:18.020
Is she intentionally making her 
presence known to McQueen?

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:22.850
McQueen!

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:23.780
McQueen!

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:24.890
McQueen...

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:28.240
The way Rice-san has her marked so 
thoroughly reminds me of something.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:31.860
It's just like when Grass-chan was 
closing in during the Takarazuka Kinen.

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:32.730
Really?

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:34.870
I think I see the similarity.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:35.770
Grass-chan?!

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:36.790
Hello there.

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:39.220
How is Rice-chan like you, though?

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:41.000
I can't say for sure.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.690
But it does feel something like fate.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:52.350
The 15 horse girls are bathed in cheers 
as they cross in front of the stands!

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.040
Settle down, McQueen!

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:55.500
Don't worry about anyone else!

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:56.810
Stick to your own pace!

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:58.480
<i>He's right.</i>

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:02.570
<i>I was able to defeat Teio last time 
because I focused on my own running.</i>

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:03.580
<i>But...</i>

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:08.340
<i>This pace... isn't suited 
to a 3,200-meter race!</i>

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:11.900
<i>I need to let my legs stay cool, so that 
I'll have enough to rush to the front!</i>

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:13.670
Go!

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:14.670
2:04?

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:15.710
Whoa, isn't that...

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:19.780
That's two seconds faster to reach the 
2,000-meter mark than the last Tennoushou!

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:21.990
Is she gonna be okay with that kind of pace?!

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:23.630
Of course she is.

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:25.650
I have faith.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.450
McQueen's gonna be okay!

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.680
Mejiro Palmer is in first place.

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:30.760
She's got a lead of five lengths.

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.520
They're now entering the 
incline on the third corner.

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:35.790
<i>More! I need to run even more!</i>

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:38.500
As they reach the third corner's incline,

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.770
they'll really begin to feel the 
Spring Tennoushou's stamina drain!

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:45.610
Whoa, and Mejiro McQueen is 
moving up on the outside!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:46.780
She's entered her spurt!

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:47.610
<i>Here she comes!</i>

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:50.280
She's closing in on Mejiro Palmer!

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.820
It's Palmer and McQueen!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:54.100
But further out, it's Rice Shower!

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:56.160
Rice Shower is moving up, too!

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.730
She's not losing her at all!

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:59.810
Is something going on with McQueen-san?

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:02.500
No, it's not McQueen.

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:05.740
Something's going on with her opponent.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.230
Go! McQueen!

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:09.810
McQueen!

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:09.620
Rice...

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:14.050
I want to run with you, too, Bourbon-san.

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:16.920
Go, Rice.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:21.930
Coming around the fourth corner,

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.620
the trio will face off down the final stretch.

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:24.940
Tannhäuser has joined them.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:27.060
But who will seize the lead?

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:32.030
It's Mejiro McQueen! Mejiro McQueen is in first!

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:33.240
Wait...

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:35.990
On the outside! On the outside!

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:39.800
It's Rice Shower! Rice Shower is closing in!

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:41.000
Look at her go!

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:44.460
<i>This pressure... but I'm not through yet!</i>

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:49.490
Rice Shower has now caught up!

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.340
Don't lose, McQueen!

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:54.380
This is McQueen's attempt 
at a third championship,

00:15:54.380 --> 00:15:58.390
but will we see Rice Shower 
thwart another accomplishment?!

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.170
Oh, come on, don't do this!

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:01.320
McQueen, you can do it!

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:04.150
Rice Shower! Are you trying 
to play the heel again?!

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:06.650
<i>I'm...</i>

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:10.690
<i>not a heel.</i>

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.160
I'm a hero!

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:32.220
Rice Shower passes her! 
Rice Shower passes her!

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.210
It's Rice Shower! She's in first!

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:37.850
The same Rice Shower who upset 
Mihono Bourbon at the Kikkashou!

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:39.850
Rice Shower has taken the lead!

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:42.590
That lead grows from two lengths to three!

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:46.560
And Rice Shower crosses 
the goal in first place!

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:50.870
McQueen...

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:53.450
Look at that time!

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.950
<b>Record</b>

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:01.320
That's a new record.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:04.210
McQueen-san...

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.920
I knew that she was strong, 
but I had no idea.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.710
I'm gonna take Rice down.

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:10.960
Impressive.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.970
<b>Record</b>

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:16.250
A record!

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:28.200
I lost.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:32.110
What the hell?

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:34.410
She did it again!

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.130
I was really looking forward 
to McQueen's third win.

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:38.140
Why's this keep happening?!

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:38.820
Unbelievable!

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:40.950
What a disappointment.

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:45.840
I shouldn't have bothered coming.

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:51.890
This is so lame.

00:18:45.590 --> 00:18:46.540
Rice...

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:57.750
Congratulations on your win, Rice.

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:02.480
I...

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:06.500
ruined a lot of people's dreams again.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:09.520
That's what it means to win.

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:11.170
It's a competition, after all.

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:16.080
If someone wins, someone else will 
be hurt, and have their dream end.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:18.210
That's just how it is.

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:21.270
Booing still hurts to hear, though.

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:24.640
It really does.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:27.820
Being booed is an honor when 
you're the challenger.

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:29.880
You don't need to feel bad about it.

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:35.670
But, one day, I'm sure it'll turn into 
cheers and words of encouragement.

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:39.420
If you keep winning, I'm sure that will happen.

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:44.850
After all, your name is Rice Shower.

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:49.600
Yeah!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:53.280
I'll do my best, okay?

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:57.530
I'd expect nothing less from my hero.

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:00.670
<b>McQueen!
Congratulations on your second place win!</b>

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.010
What a feast!

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:03.510
It certainly is.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.850
Spe-senpai! Time out for now!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.440
Huh? Where's McQueen?

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:12.440
Good point. It didn't end up being 
a celebration, but we still need our star.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:14.990
Could you go find her, Teio?

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:16.400
Yeah, sure.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:17.400
Hey.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:20.200
Take these.

00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:38.830
McQueen, you ran a fine race.

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:41.130
Yes, likewise.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:43.970
It's a shame your streak was broken.

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.970
You're bringing that up, too?

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:49.890
Everyone on my team has 
been so considerate.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:52.820
And I'd be lying if I said it didn't bother me,

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:54.960
but I'm not really that upset.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:59.160
Really? You seemed a bit lonely.

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:04.510
I do feel a bit guilty.

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:05.840
Guilty?

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:09.200
Yes. For disappointing the fans who were 
cheering me on, of course,

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:10.860
but for disappointing Tokai Teio in particular.

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:15.180
Teio is working hard to 
complete her rehabilitation.

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:21.080
With her goal being to race against me,
 an unbeatable horse girl.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:25.570
And yet, my performance 
was less than adequate.

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:31.970
I will run in a way that 
makes me fit to be your goal.

00:21:33.130 --> 00:21:34.360
McQueen...

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:40.200
Overconfidence in my knack 
for handling the race's distance...

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:42.340
A false sense of security,
due to it being my third time...

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:45.380
And most of all, the fact
that I was arrogant enough

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:46.940
to think I was racing for Teio's sake...

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:48.650
It's no wonder I lost.

00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:55.700
I was simply less focused 
on victory than Rice Shower.

00:21:56.890 --> 00:21:59.880
But I won't make the same mistake again.

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:03.360
I need to maintain 
my position as the strongest.

00:22:03.980 --> 00:22:07.650
At the Takarazuka Kinen, I will win.

00:22:07.650 --> 00:22:09.010
McQueen...

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:13.720
My rotation has me running in the Yasuda Kinen,
 and then the Takarazuka Kinen.

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:18.600
We'll be racing. And I don't 
intend to let you win.

00:22:19.280 --> 00:22:21.990
I'm truly blessed.

00:22:21.990 --> 00:22:24.950
I have so many rivals...

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:34.240
<i>The Takarazuka Kinen!</i>
